'''''Moricandia arvensis''''', the '''purple mistress''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Brassicaceae]].<ref name="GBIF_5376035">{{cite web |title=''Moricandia arvensis'' (L.) DC. |url=https://www.gbif.org/species/5376035 |website=gbif.org |publisher=GBIF Secretariat |author=GBIF Backbone Taxonomy. |access-date=9 January 2022 }}</ref> It has a broadly western Mediterranean distribution, from the Canary Islands to northern Africa including Mauritania and Chad, the Iberian Peninsula, Italy and as far as Greece, and has been introduced to France, Corsica, and Sardinia.<ref name="1085378-2">{{cite POWO |id=1085378-2 |title=''Moricandia arvensis'' (L.) DC. |access-date=9 January 2022 }}</ref> It has an intermediate [[C3 carbon fixation|C{{sub|3}}]]–[[C4 carbon fixation|C{{sub|4}} carbon fixation]] system,<ref name="1_of_2150_Google_Scholar_hits">{{cite journal |title=Anatomical, ultrastructural and enzymic studies of leaves of ''Moricandia arvensis'', a C{{sub|3}}-C{{sub|4}} intermediate species |year=1981 |last1=Holaday |first1=A.Scott |last2=Shieh |first2=Yuh-Jang |last3=Lee |first3=Kit W. |last4=Chollet |first4=Raymond |journal=Biochimica et Biophysica Acta (BBA) - Bioenergetics |volume=637 |issue=2 |pages=334–341 |doi=10.1016/0005-2728(81)90172-9 }}</ref> known as [[C2 photosynthesis|C{{sub|2}} photosynthesis]].<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Adwy |first1=W |last2=Laxa |first2=M |last3=Peterhansel |first3=C |title=A simple mechanism for the establishment of C₂-specific gene expression in Brassicaceae. |journal=The Plant Journal |date=December 2015 |volume=84 |issue=6 |pages=1231–8 |doi=10.1111/tpj.13084 |pmid=26603271 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

